<ul>
<li>The ethylene is partially inserted into the Zr-CH3 bond</li>
<li>There's a 4-membered ring with Zr-C(ethylene)-C(ethylene)-C(methyl)</li=
>
<li>Both the Zr-CH3 bond and one of the Zr-ethylene bonds are being broken/=
formed</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Product</strong>: A zirconocene cation with:</p>
<ul>
<li>Two Cp ligands</li>
<li>A propyl group (CH2-CH2-CH3) attached to Zr</li>
</ul>
<p>This is an important reaction in Ziegler-Natta polymerization mechanism.=
</p>
